{"title":"Even integer","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>An <b>even integer</b> is any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> which is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Multiple\" title=\"Multiple\">multiple</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  The even integers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b54c47e32327c987e20e97823808513f1c28fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots, -4, -2, 0, 2, 4, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"16\" />; specifically, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is even. Every even integer can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> for some unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The sum and difference of any two integers with the same <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parity\" title=\"Parity\">parity</a> is even.\nThe product of any two even integers is not only even but is also <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisible\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Divisible\">divisible</a> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  The sum of an even integer and an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd_integer\" title=\"Odd integer\">odd integer</a> is odd.  \n</p><p>Since every even integer is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the only <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> even integer.\n</p><p>The number of even integers are in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc4cb4d41cf554d0db7d1dac17dc55c527c1431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7453b63587815988dd1001a3dfba3e50a5812d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac {|x|}{2}\\right\\rfloor+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"78\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Even_integer&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017151600\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 277/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1763/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.652      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.652      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3966:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017151600 and revision id 186974. Ren